{"nodes": [{"id": "changelog_document", "label": "CHANGELOG.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_calibration_bug", "label": "O-03-BLG235 frozen PSPL flux-calibration bug", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "preprocess_binary_data.py's one-time PSPL-based flux calibration (fs_ogle/fb_ogle/fs_moa) was frozen and reused for every downstream fit including the 2L1S search. Evaluating chi2 at Bond et al. 2004's real published parameters gave 31,982 under the frozen calibration vs. 1,953 once fs/fb are re-solved analytically per trial against the true trajectory -- frozen values were off by 40%+, with fb_ogle even wrong-signed. This calibration bug, not a search-algorithm problem, was the real reason every 2L1S search kept landing in the wrong basin (session 4's initial conclusion was itself wrong)."}, {"id": "changelog_u0_sign_bug", "label": "u0 mirror-image sign bug", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PSPL's u0 only enters the model squared, so curve_fit can converge to the mirror-image (wrong-sign) solution from a bad initial guess. Hit for real when consolidating two MCMC scripts: one dataset's hardcoded u0 guess was silently reused for another, producing a wrong-sign, artificially tight posterior that still looked converged; chi2 didn't flag it. Lesson: per-dataset fit configuration (initial guesses) is not safe to treat as a shared constant."}, {"id": "changelog_near_miss_cusp_problem", "label": "Non-physical near-miss cusp solutions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Once the flux-calibration bug was fixed, chi2 minimization began favoring non-physical 'near-miss cusp' trajectories (no 3->5 image-count/caustic-crossing transition) that score numerically better than Bond et al.'s own published parameters. Only the image-count/caustic check catches these, not chi2 alone; 3 of 4 independent 2L1S searches (joint multi-start, both MOA-only searches) converged to such artifacts, blocking the planned BIC-vs-PSPL verdict."}, {"id": "changelog_error_bar_underestimation", "label": "MOA-2019-BLG-008 KMT error-bar underestimation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Raw KMTNet/pySIS mag_err column (median 0.006 mag) understates the real point-to-point scatter (~0.1-0.2 mag) by roughly 16-49x, confirmed model-independently via a flat-line baseline fit (chi2/dof=2441 with no lensing model at all). A known property of raw KMTNet pipeline photometry; every published microlensing analysis rescales error bars before fitting. This, not the physical model or search algorithm, is why fit_2l1s_moa19008.py's first run produced uniformly bad chi2/dof (~100-350) regardless of trial parameters."}, {"id": "changelog_bic_verdict", "label": "BIC-based PSPL-vs-2L1S model comparison verdict", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_alpha_gap_discrepancy", "label": "Unresolved ~15deg alpha discrepancy vs Bond et al. 2004", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The current best validated 2L1S solution for O-03-BLG235 (chi2=1825.35, alpha~209.2deg, joint MCMC best sample tight-refined) is a genuine caustic crossing and scores better than Bond et al.'s own chi2 (1952.9), but its alpha is still ~15deg off Bond's published 223.8deg -- an open discrepancy not yet chased down."}, {"id": "changelog_mulensmodel_alpha_convention_bug", "label": "MulensModel alpha-convention cross-check bug", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A first cross-check against MulensModel showed 1-6% (far-field) up to ~250x (near-caustic) disagreement with binary_magnification, which looked like a real physics bug. It was actually a coordinate-convention bug in the comparison script itself: MulensModel's own alpha convention is shifted 180deg from what was assumed, confirmed empirically rather than trusted from the docstring. Explicitly called out as the same category of failure as the u0 sign bug: a wrong-but-plausible result that superficially looks like the thing being tested for."}, {"id": "changelog_wyrzykowski_2015", "label": "Wyrzykowski et al. 2015", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_bond_et_al_2004", "label": "Bond et al. 2004 (arXiv:astro-ph/0404309)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_kass_raftery", "label": "Kass & Raftery (BIC/Bayes-factor interpretation)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_han_gould_2003", "label": "Han & Gould 2003", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_bachelet_2022", "label"